CURRICULUM SERVER

IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT: CENTRALIZED GEMINI TEXTBOOK GENERATION GOVERNANCE AND CONTROL PLANE

PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Implement a production-ready, centrally governed AI Textbook Generation Management System within Curriculum Server.

The system must use Gemini AI to generate comprehensive, academically accurate, developmentally appropriate and visually consistent textbooks based on the authoritative NERDC curriculum stored in the central curriculum database.

The most important architectural requirement is:

The Super Admin must have complete centralized control over Gemini textbook generation rules, independently configurable for every subject and every class or educational level, through the Curriculum Server Control Plane.

The configuration must control how Gemini generates:

1. Educational context.
2. Textbook content.
3. Chapter and topic structures.
4. Definitions and explanations.
5. Examples and worked examples.
6. Graphical illustrations.
7. Diagrams, charts and graphs.
8. Verbal descriptions and captions accompanying illustrations.
9. Practical exercises and learning activities.
10. Assessment questions and answer keys.
11. Chapter summaries and revision materials.

The system must guarantee that all these components are appropriate for the assigned educational level, class, subject and applicable NERDC curriculum.

This is an implementation task, not a proposal or documentation exercise.

Inspect the existing Curriculum Server project and integrate the implementation into its actual architecture.

Preserve existing functionality and avoid introducing a competing textbook generation engine.

