PART 2: CENTRAL NERDC CURRICULUM DATABASE INTEGRATION

2.1 Authoritative curriculum source

The existing central NERDC curriculum database must remain the authoritative source of curriculum information.

Do not create another NERDC curriculum database.

Do not duplicate curriculum records unnecessarily.

Before every textbook generation operation, retrieve the applicable:

- Curriculum framework.
- Curriculum version.
- Educational level.
- Class.
- Subject.
- Strand.
- Sub-strand.
- Topic.
- Subtopic.
- Learning objectives.
- Expected learning outcomes.
- Competencies.
- Prerequisite knowledge, where available.

The retrieved curriculum information must be passed to Gemini as trusted generation context.

2.2 Curriculum-to-textbook traceability

Every generated chapter and topic must reference the applicable curriculum records.

Every generated learning activity and assessment must be traceable to the learning objectives it supports.

Every significant illustration must reference its relevant topic and learning objective.

The engine must maintain a curriculum coverage record showing:

- Total applicable learning objectives.
- Objectives covered.
- Objectives partially covered.
- Objectives not covered.
- Associated textbook chapters.
- Associated assessments.
- Associated illustrations.

Do not claim complete curriculum coverage when mandatory objectives remain uncovered.

2.3 Curriculum version management

Each generated textbook must record the exact curriculum version used.

If the curriculum changes, do not silently modify previously approved textbooks.

Flag affected textbook editions for review and controlled regeneration.

